---
import SetupLayout from '../../../layouts/SetupLayout.astro';
import { Terminal, Monitor, Apple, Download, CheckCircle } from '@lucide/astro';
---
<SetupLayout title="Spectrum with Pasmo" description="Alternative local tools for this machine’s assembly lessons." systemSlug="sinclair-zx-spectrum" alternative>
  <p>This guide uses Pasmo. For the recommended Asm198x workflow and available browser lessons, use the <a href="/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum/getting-started/">main setup guide</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="install">Install the alternative tools</h2>
    <section class="tabs-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="tabs-wrapper" data-setup-tabs>
          <div class="tab-bar" role="tablist" aria-label="Operating system">
            <button class="tab active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="macos" id="tab-macos" aria-controls="macos" tabindex="0" type="button">
              <Apple size={20} />
              <span>macOS</span>
            </button>
            <button class="tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="windows" id="tab-windows" aria-controls="windows" tabindex="-1" type="button">
              <Monitor size={20} />
              <span>Windows</span>
            </button>
            <button class="tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="linux" id="tab-linux" aria-controls="linux" tabindex="-1" type="button">
              <Terminal size={20} />
              <span>Linux</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <!-- macOS Panel -->
          <div class="tab-panel active" id="macos" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-macos" tabindex="0"><h3 class="os-heading">macOS</h3>
            <div class="install-steps">
              <div class="step">
                <h3>1. Install Homebrew (if needed)</h3>
                <div class="code-block" tabindex="0">
                  <code>/bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"</code>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="step">
                <h3>2. Install Pasmo Assembler</h3>
                <div class="code-block" tabindex="0">
                  <code>brew install pasmo</code>
                </div>
                <p class="step-note">The curriculum's sources use Pasmo notation, and Pasmo builds them as they are. Asm198x builds the same program bytes.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="step">
                <h3>3. Install Emu198x</h3>
                <p>With Homebrew, run <code>brew install emu198x/tap/emu198x-spectrum</code>.</p>
                <p>Or download the <code>emu198x-spectrum</code> archive for your Mac from the <a href="https://github.com/emu198x/emu198x/releases/latest">latest Emu198x release</a>: <code>aarch64-apple-darwin</code> for Apple silicon, <code>x86_64-apple-darwin</code> for Intel. Extract it into a folder you can find again.</p>
                <p class="step-note">The release notes include checksums. The emulator needs a 48K Spectrum ROM; see <a href="#run">Running your code</a>.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="step">
                <h3>4. Verify Installation</h3>
                <div class="code-block" tabindex="0">
                  <code>pasmo --version</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Windows Panel -->
          <div class="tab-panel" id="windows" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-windows" tabindex="0"><h3 class="os-heading">Windows</h3>
            <div class="install-steps">
              <div class="step">
                <h3>1. Download Pasmo</h3>
                <p>Download pasmo from <a href="http://pasmo.speccy.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pasmo.speccy.org</a>.</p>
                <p class="step-note">Extract to a folder like <code>C:\Tools\pasmo</code> and add it to your PATH.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="step">
                <h3>2. Install Emu198x</h3>
                <p>Download the <code>emu198x-spectrum</code> <code>x86_64-pc-windows-msvc</code> zip from the <a href="https://github.com/emu198x/emu198x/releases/latest">latest Emu198x release</a> and extract it into a folder such as <code>C:\Tools\emu198x</code>.</p>
                <p class="step-note">The release notes include checksums. The emulator needs a 48K Spectrum ROM; see <a href="#run">Running your code</a>.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="step">
                <h3>3. Verify Installation</h3>
                <div class="code-block" tabindex="0">
                  <code>pasmo --version</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Linux Panel -->
          <div class="tab-panel" id="linux" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-linux" tabindex="0"><h3 class="os-heading">Linux</h3>
            <div class="install-steps">
              <div class="step">
                <h3>1. Install Pasmo (Debian/Ubuntu)</h3>
                <div class="code-block" tabindex="0">
                  <code>sudo apt install pasmo</code>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="step">
                <h3>2. Install Emu198x</h3>
                <p>If you use Homebrew on Linux, run <code>brew install emu198x/tap/emu198x-spectrum</code>.</p>
                <p>Or download the <code>emu198x-spectrum</code> archive: <code>aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu</code> for ARM64, or <code>x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu</code> for x86-64, from the <a href="https://github.com/emu198x/emu198x/releases/latest">latest Emu198x release</a> and extract it into a folder you can find again.</p>
                <p class="step-note">The release notes include checksums. The emulator needs a 48K Spectrum ROM; see <a href="#run">Running your code</a>.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="step">
                <h3>3. Verify Installation</h3>
                <div class="code-block" tabindex="0">
                  <code>pasmo --version</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Build Example -->
    <section class="install-section alt" id="run">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Building Your Code</h2>
        <p class="section-description">Once installed, build your assembly files directly:</p>

        <div class="code-block large" tabindex="0">
          <code>pasmo --tapbas game.asm game.tap</code>
        </div>

        <h2>Running Your Code</h2>
        <p class="section-description">Emu198x needs a lawfully obtained 48K Spectrum ROM; the <a href="/setup/roms/">ROM guide</a> explains what firmware is and how to obtain it. For an archive, open a terminal in the folder where you extracted Emu198x. With Homebrew, omit <code>./</code> from the command below and run it from your project folder. On macOS or Linux, this loads the tape and runs it:</p>

        <div class="code-block large" tabindex="0">
          <code>./emu198x-spectrum --rom "path/to/48.rom" --tape game.tap --autoload-tape</code>
        </div>

        <p class="section-description">In Windows PowerShell:</p>

        <div class="code-block large" tabindex="0">
          <code>.\emu198x-spectrum.exe --rom "C:\path\to\48.rom" --tape game.tap --autoload-tape</code>
        </div>

        <p class="section-description">Replace the paths with your ROM and tape locations, keeping the quotes if a path contains spaces. <code>--autoload-tape</code> waits for the Spectrum to start, types <code>LOAD ""</code> and plays the tape. Without it, enter <code>LOAD ""</code> yourself and press F9 to start the tape.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Back Link -->
    <section class="back-section">
      <div class="container">
        <a href="/setup" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Setup Guide</a>
        <a href="/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum" class="start-link">Start the Spectrum Curriculum &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

</SetupLayout>
<script src="../../../scripts/setup-tabs.ts"></script>
